  "metaDescription": "The East Jakarta District Court has scheduled the next session in the trial of Roy Suryo concerning allegations against the former president's diploma.",
  "aiSummaryBullets": [
    "The East Jakarta District Court has set the next trial date for the Roy Suryo case involving allegations of falsified documents for November 25, 2026.",
    "Legal counsel for the defendant has requested that prosecutors summon specific witnesses who have previously failed to appear in court.",
    "Defense arguments currently focus on discrepancies regarding signatures on document legalizations and verification procedures conducted by election officials."
  ],
  "aiContextParagraph": "The legal proceedings against Roy Suryo, currently before the East Jakarta District Court, relate to allegations concerning the academic credentials of former President Joko Widodo. Recent court sessions have focused on testimony regarding the verification processes of the diploma, with defense counsel questioning officials from the General Election Commission about inconsistencies in document legalization procedures from 2014 and 2019. The defense has also petitioned the prosecution to present witnesses who have missed multiple court appearances. While the prosecution maintains the validity of the documents, the case remains an ongoing matter in the judiciary. The former president has previously requested the restoration of his reputation following the public claims. The court has now formally recessed, with the next session expected to resume at the end of November 2026 to further address witness presentations and evidence examination.",
